  (7,15,20) s=21 (x,y,z)=(14,6,1) (x+y+z)xyz=1764 =? A^2=1764  True
  (9,10,17) s=18 (x,y,z)=(9,8,1) (x+y+z)xyz=1296 =? A^2=1296  True
naturals 0..199 NOT a sum of 4 squares (Lagrange): [] (empty => theorem holds)
naturals 0..199 NOT a sum of 3 triangular (Gauss):  [] (empty => EYPHKA holds)

The recursive duality: square = PRODUCT of 4 naturals (Heron, glue=sum),
natural = SUM of 4 squares (Lagrange); '4'=2^2 (parity squared), '3'=triangle sides.

